{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"e005b97419e747d2b8415f686c2482a625a2952f8a6578a4a82a5cca755ffde1","digest":{"component_or_area":"signing seam and attestation verification","key_entities":["src/rebar/signing.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py","src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_engine_support/validate.py","signing.sign_manifest()","signing.verify_record()","sign_opcert_manifest()","opcert_from_record()","attest.registry.verify()",".opcert-key",".opcert-key.pub","rebar.opcert.v1","REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID","sign_result.schema.json","verify_signature_result.schema.json","SignResultOut","SIGNATURE event","attestations[kind]"],"problem_keywords":["producer signing","Ed25519 op-certs","DSSE envelope","environment key","expand phase","read-both","key genesis","HMAC to op-cert migration"],"propositions":["The sign_manifest seam must be globally repointed to mint rebar.opcert.v1 DSSE op-certs with the ambient environment's Ed25519 key, replacing the legacy per-clone HMAC secret signing across five enumerated call sites (plan-review producer, drift-refresh producer, resign, rebar sign CLI, MCP sign_manifest tool).","On first signing use, generate a passphrase-free Ed25519 keypair at <tracker>/.opcert-key via race-safe exclusive-create (0700 staging dir, os.link private key as sole commit point), with derivative .pub written only after the private key is committed; verify-side never creates a key.","The expand-phase read path must dispatch on record shape: envelope-bearing records route to op-cert verification via the attest registry; legacy signature-bearing records route to unchanged HMAC verification; a foreign-key record (principal != environment id) is classified without invoking the scheme.","Expand-phase sign_result.schema.json and SignResultOut must admit both legacy HMAC shape (signature field) and envelope-bearing shape (envelope, principal, algorithm fields) to support coexistence during the migration.","When ssh-keygen is unavailable or the key is unreadable and cannot be regenerated, signing records the in-band {signed: false, error: …} outcome without blocking the local operation; the gated producer then blocks at the gate with an install-OpenSSH remediation message.","Close-gate producer and all validity-on-read lifecycle rules (reopen, code drift, material drift) apply unchanged to envelope attestations; never-sign guards (non-PASS, degraded coverage, certifiable: false, source=='local') remain enforced."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785821797406859767,"uuid":"927a0779-2b33-406a-b095-4177eff3481f"}